Q4. Consider the following code fragment:
int a=0;
if (fork() == 0)
{ a = a + 5; printf(“%d,%d\n”, a, &a); }
else { a = a –5; printf(“%d, %d\n”, a, &a); }
What will be the relationship (if any) between the two values printed by the child process and the corresponding values printed by the parent process.

Q5. What should be the maximum Page size and TLB Size in your system so that pretty much every access in the below code leads to a TLB miss? Assume that TLB is empty to begin with and uses LRU policy. Also the data array is page aligned (i.e stored starting from the 0th byte of a given page frame) and size of int to be 4 bytes. Explain your answer.
int value = 0; 
int data[50][2048]; // a big array 
for (int j = 0; j <N; j++) { 
    for (int i = 0; i <M; i++) { 
value = value + data[i][j]; 
    }
}
